        "LocalizationKey": "CMC_InnKeeperTalk_Week3_Backstory2_Line",
        "DefaultText": "My father dug the cellar with his own two hands, and my mother never turned a traveler from the door once the dark caught them out. Word spread. More came to stay than we had room for, so we raised walls around the hearth, then a roof, then the Inn you're sitting in now. I've been thinking it's time this place grew again. The village could use more hands, and truth is, I could use help seeing it done."
